    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0534" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg486"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. de Stoeckl</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 24, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Will Mr. de Stoeckl have the goodness to recall the attention of the imperial
                    government to the request which the United States government has made for
                    explanations concerning the alleged proceedings or regulations affecting the
                    freedom of the fisheries in the Sea of Okhotsk? The subject is not unlikely to
                    produce present uneasiness, which would soon be inconvenient, and ultimately
                    become a source of regret.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to offer to you the renewed assurance of my very
                    high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward de Stoeckl</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
